   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch4/q6",
   "question": "<p>The roots of the quartic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3x^4+5x^3-7x+6=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\delta\"></span></p><p>Making your method clear and without solving the equation, determine the exact value of</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2+\\delta^2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{2}{\\alpha}+\\dfrac{2}{\\beta}+\\dfrac{2}{\\gamma}+\\dfrac{2}{\\delta}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3-\\alpha)(3-\\beta)(3-\\gamma)(3-\\delta)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
